\f1\fs20 "Faith is the great cop-out, the great excuse to evade the need to think and evaluate evidence. Faith is belief in spite of, even perhaps because of, the lack of evidence."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Religion is capable of driving people to such dangerous folly that faith seems to me to qualify as a kind of mental illness."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Religion is about turning untested belief into unshakable truth through the power of institutions and the passage of time."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We are all atheists about most of the gods that humanity has ever believed in. Some of us just go one god further."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The God of the Old Testament is arguably the most unpleasant character in all fiction: jealous and proud of it; a petty, unjust, unforgiving control-freak; a vindictive, bloodthirsty ethnic cleanser; a misogynistic, homophobic, racist, infanticidal, genocidal, filicidal, pestilential, megalomaniacal, sadomasochistic, capriciously malevolent bully.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Science replaces private prejudice with publicly verifiable evidence."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"To be an atheist is a realistic aspiration, and a brave and splendid one. You can be an atheist who is happy, balanced, moral, and intellectually fulfilled."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Faith can be very very dangerous, and deliberately to implant it into the vulnerable mind of an innocent child is a grievous wrong.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The meme for blind faith secures its own perpetuation by the simple unconscious expedient of discouraging rational inquiry."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We are survival machines \'96 robot vehicles blindly programmed to preserve the selfish molecules known as genes. This is a truth which still fills me with astonishment."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Natural selection is the blind watchmaker, blind because it does not see ahead, does not plan consequences, has no purpose in view. Yet the living results of natural selection overwhelmingly impress us with the appearance of design as if by a master watchmaker."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The universe we observe has precisely the properties we should expect if there is, at bottom, no design, no purpose, no evil, no good, nothing but blind, pitiless indifference."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The fact that life evolved out of nearly nothing, some 10 billion years after the universe evolved out of literally nothing, is a fact so staggering that I would be mad to attempt words to do it justice."\
